WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:15.925
Unit thirty-two: Reported Speech (introduction). Today you will tell other people what someone said.

4
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:19.051
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.291
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:24.849
Said.

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.675
Said means the past of say.

8
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:30.016
She said that she was tired.

9
00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:33.118
Your turn. Say: Said.

10
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:36.840
Said.

11
00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:38.364
Told.

12
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.895
Told means the past of tell, used with a person.

13
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:43.821
She told me a story.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:46.709
Your turn. Say: Told.

15
00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:50.359
Told.

16
00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.443
Reported speech.

17
00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:56.483
Reported speech means words that tell what someone said.

18
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.187
Reported speech changes the tense.

19
00:00:59.783 --> 00:01:02.970
Your turn. Say: Reported speech.

20
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:07.287
Reported speech.

21
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:09.307
Direct speech.

22
00:01:10.317 --> 00:01:13.558
Direct speech means the exact words that someone says.

23
00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.579
Direct speech uses quotation marks.

24
00:01:17.183 --> 00:01:20.335
Your turn. Say: Direct speech.

25
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.584
Direct speech.

26
00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:26.328
Backshift.

27
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:30.048
Backshift means moving the tense one step back.

28
00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.917
Backshift changes am into was.

29
00:01:33.517 --> 00:01:35.821
Your turn. Say: Backshift.

30
00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:39.645
Backshift.

31
00:01:40.383 --> 00:01:41.025
That.

32
00:01:42.017 --> 00:01:44.864
That means a word that can introduce reported speech.

33
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.194
She said that she was tired.

34
00:01:47.783 --> 00:01:50.529
Your turn. Say: That.

35
00:01:53.367 --> 00:01:54.391
That.

36
00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.209
Yesterday.

37
00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.390
Yesterday means the day before today.

38
00:01:59.983 --> 00:02:01.809
She said she saw him yesterday.

39
00:02:02.417 --> 00:02:05.150
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

40
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.082
Yesterday.

41
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:10.899
The next day.

42
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.777
The next day means the day after the day in the past.

43
00:02:15.383 --> 00:02:17.394
He said he would come the next day.

44
00:02:17.983 --> 00:02:20.670
Your turn. Say: The next day.

45
00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:24.592
The next day.

46
00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:28.853
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:33.170
Visal, your teacher said 'I am happy.' How do you report it?

48
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:45.632
The teacher said that she was happy. In reported speech, we usually move the tense one step back: am becomes was, work becomes worked, will becomes would.

49
00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.345
What about time words?

50
00:02:49.450 --> 00:03:02.505
They change too: today becomes that day, tomorrow becomes the next day, yesterday becomes the day before. Pronouns also change: I becomes she or he.

51
00:03:03.617 --> 00:03:04.769
Say or tell?

52
00:03:05.883 --> 00:03:18.221
We use told with a person: She told me she was tired. We use said without one: She said she was tired. That is optional: She said (that) she was tired.

53
00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.215
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.000
Grammar focus: Reported speech: said (that) plus backshift.

55
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.498
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:28.183 --> 00:03:29.927
She said that she was tired.

57
00:03:30.817 --> 00:03:32.851
He told me that he worked in a bank.

58
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.819
They said that they would come the next day.

59
00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:47.456
Use said (that) or told + person (that). Move the tense one step back: am → was, work → worked, will → would. Change pronouns and time words.

60
00:03:48.217 --> 00:03:51.380
Be careful! Don't say: She said me that she was ill.

61
00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.041
Say: She told me that she was ill.

62
00:03:56.341 --> 00:03:57.946
Use told with a person.

63
00:03:58.733 --> 00:04:01.339
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:03.192
What Did They Say?.

65
00:04:03.492 --> 00:04:05.991
My teacher said that she was happy with our work.

66
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.023
My friend told me that he worked in a bank.

67
00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.172
They said that they would come the next day.

68
00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:14.922
She said that she had seen the film.

69
00:04:15.933 --> 00:04:18.792
Reported speech tells us what someone else said.

70
00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:24.366
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:25.217 --> 00:04:29.053
She said, 'I am tired.' → She said she blank tired.

72
00:04:29.353 --> 00:04:32.310
A, is. B, was. C, were.

73
00:04:35.867 --> 00:04:37.553
The answer is B: was.

74
00:04:38.717 --> 00:04:40.670
He blank me that he was busy.

75
00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:44.182
A, said. B, told. C, say.

76
00:04:47.733 --> 00:04:49.431
The answer is B: told.

77
00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:52.943
'Tomorrow' becomes blank in reported speech.

78
00:04:53.243 --> 00:04:57.303
A, the next day. B, yesterday. C, today.

79
00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:03.145
The answer is A: the next day.

80
00:05:04.283 --> 00:05:05.818
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:06.118 --> 00:05:11.571
A, She said me she was ill.. B, She told me she was ill.. C, She told that she was ill..

82
00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:17.992
The answer is B: She told me she was ill..

83
00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.985
According to the reading, what did the teacher say?

84
00:05:22.285 --> 00:05:27.123
A, she was happy with the work. B, she was late. C, she was ill.

85
00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.398
The answer is A: she was happy with the work.

86
00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:37.949
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:38.783 --> 00:05:41.003
Tell a friend what your teacher said today.

88
00:05:49.817 --> 00:05:51.282
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:51.582 --> 00:06:01.435
My teacher said that we would have a test next week. She told us that we should review the units. In reported speech I change the tense and I use said or told.

90
00:06:01.735 --> 00:06:03.433
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:04.317 --> 00:06:09.930
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech: said (that) plus backshift.

92
00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:14.426
Today's value is truthfulness. Tell the truth and check the facts.

93
00:06:14.726 --> 00:06:17.761
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

94
00:06:18.061 --> 00:06:20.946
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

